    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>A house and table d'hôtes tucked away in the Nice hinterland, in the village of L'Escarène, about thirty minutes from Nice. More than two hectares of grounds surround the property.</p>

      <h2>What to know before you book</h2>
      <p>An important point to check first: two directories specialising in dog-friendly accommodation stated a free welcome (up to two dogs under 30kg, no breed restriction). But the establishment's official website (lorigane.com/infos) currently shows the opposite policy: "animals not accepted", due to unfenced grounds and a risk of conflict with the dogs and cats already living on site. This policy has likely changed since the directories indexed their listing — the official, current source should take priority. Call before booking to confirm, do not rely on the directories alone on this point.</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: even if the policy has changed, these more-than-2-hectare grounds remain a lovely address for a stay without your dog in the Nice hinterland — but check by phone first before making the trip with your companion.</div>

      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>The village of L'Escarène, with its 17th-century bridge, can be visited on foot, and the Paillon valley offers several hiking trails accessible with a dog.</p>
